  "hindi": "तेज़ दधिक्रा की हम अब स्तुति करें, और आकाश से और पृथ्वी से उसका बार-बार कीर्तन करेंगे। प्रकाशित होती हुई उषाएँ मुझे ठीक करें; वे सब संकटों के पार ले चलें।",
  "english": "Let us now praise him, the swift Dadhikrā, and we shall celebrate him from heaven and from earth. May the dawning Dawns set me right; may they carry across all troubles.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "divaḥ pṛthivyāḥ may be ablative ('from heaven and earth') or genitive ('of Heaven and Earth'); the ablative is used here. parṣan is read as 3 pl. subjunctive with ati; the object of the carrying is not expressed, so none is added. carkirāma is a subjunctive of the intensive of √kṝ 'celebrate'.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
