  "hindi": "मैं अश्व की महिमा का कीर्तन करता हूँ, संकल्प को पूर्ण करने वाले, बहुत वरणीय धन वाले, बलवान् दधिक्रावन् की; जिसे पूरुओं के लिए अग्नि के समान चमकते हुए, विजयी को, हे मित्र और वरुण, तुम दोनों ने दिया।",
  "english": "I celebrate the greatness of the steed, of Dadhikrāvan who fulfils resolve, rich in many treasures, of the bull; him whom, shining like Agni, the conqueror, you two, Mitra and Varuṇa, gave for the Pūrus.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "mahaḥ is read as the neuter noun 'greatness' (acc.). puru-vāra: vāra may be 'treasure, desirable thing' or 'tail'; the first is used. kratuprāḥ: the printed kratuprā is the genitive kratuprāḥ with regular loss of the visarga before d-. Mitrāvaruṇā is the dual vocative of the pair.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
